---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy — ZeroMotion" description="ZeroMotion Marketing Cookie Policy - Detailed information about our cookie usage, categories, purposes, and how to manage your cookie preferences.">
  <main class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-page max-w-4xl">
      <h1 class="h2 mb-6">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-white/85 mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        This Cookie Policy explains how ZeroMotion Marketing uses cookies and similar technologies on our website. We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content. This policy explains what cookies are, how we use them, and your rights to control them.
      </p>

      <div class="card p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-4 text-primary">Last Updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</h2>
        <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
          This Cookie Policy is part of our overall Privacy Policy and should be read together with it. By using our website, you consent to the use of cookies in accordance with this policy.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-primary/10 p-4 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-white/85 text-sm">
            <strong>Quick Action:</strong> You can manage your cookie preferences at any time by clicking "Cookie Settings" in the footer of any page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">1. What Are Cookies?</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Cookie Definition</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
              Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer or mobile device when you visit a website. They allow the website to remember your actions and preferences over a period of time, so you don't have to keep re-entering them whenever you come back to the site or browse from one page to another.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Types of Cookies We Use</h3>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">First-party Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Set directly by our website</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Third-party Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Set by third-party services we use</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Session Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Temporary, deleted when you close browser</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Persistent Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Remain until deleted or expired</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">2. Cookie Categories</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card p-6 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-4 h-4 bg-green-500 rounded-full mt-1 flex-shrink-0"></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-green-400">Essential Cookies (Always Active)</h3>
                <p class="text-white/85 mb-3">
                  These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services.
                </p>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Purpose:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Website security and fraud prevention</li>
                  <li>• User authentication and session management</li>
                  <li>• Load balancing and server optimization</li>
                  <li>• Remembering your cookie consent preferences</li>
                  <li>• Basic website functionality</li>
                </ul>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 mt-3 text-white/90">Examples:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Session identifiers</li>
                  <li>• CSRF protection tokens</li>
                  <li>• Load balancer cookies</li>
                  <li>• Consent management cookies</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-yellow-500/30 bg-yellow-500/5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-4 h-4 bg-yellow-500 rounded-full mt-1 flex-shrink-0"></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-yellow-400">Analytics Cookies</h3>
                <p class="text-white/85 mb-3">
                  These cookies help us understand how visitors interact with our website by collecting and reporting information anonymously. This helps us improve our website's performance and user experience.
                </p>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Purpose:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Track page views and user navigation patterns</li>
                  <li>• Measure website performance and loading times</li>
                  <li>• Identify popular content and user preferences</li>
                  <li>• Detect technical issues and bugs</li>
                  <li>• Generate anonymous usage statistics</li>
                </ul>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 mt-3 text-white/90">Providers:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Google Analytics 4 (anonymized data)</li>
                  <li>• Microsoft Clarity (user experience insights)</li>
                  <li>• Hotjar (behavioral analytics)</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="mt-3 p-3 bg-yellow-500/10 rounded">
                  <p class="text-white/75 text-sm"><strong>Note:</strong> All analytics data is anonymized and aggregated. We do not use analytics cookies to identify individual users.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-4 h-4 bg-blue-500 rounded-full mt-1 flex-shrink-0"></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-blue-400">Marketing Cookies</h3>
                <p class="text-white/85 mb-3">
                  These cookies are used to track visitors across websites to display relevant and engaging advertisements. They remember that you've visited our website and share this information with advertising partners.
                </p>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Purpose:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Display relevant advertisements</li>
                  <li>• Measure advertising campaign effectiveness</li>
                  <li>• Retargeting and remarketing</li>
                  <li>• Cross-device advertising</li>
                  <li>• Audience segmentation</li>
                </ul>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 mt-3 text-white/90">Providers:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Facebook Pixel (social media advertising)</li>
                  <li>• LinkedIn Insight Tag (professional networking)</li>
                  <li>• Google Ads (search and display advertising)</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="mt-3 p-3 bg-blue-500/10 rounded">
                  <p class="text-white/75 text-sm"><strong>Control:</strong> You can opt-out of marketing cookies at any time using our cookie settings or by adjusting your browser preferences.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6 border-purple-500/30 bg-purple-500/5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-4 h-4 bg-purple-500 rounded-full mt-1 flex-shrink-0"></div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-purple-400">Functional Cookies</h3>
                <p class="text-white/85 mb-3">
                  These cookies enable enhanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third-party providers whose services we have added to our pages.
                </p>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Purpose:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Remember your preferences and settings</li>
                  <li>• Enable social media features</li>
                  <li>• Provide live chat functionality</li>
                  <li>• Remember form data across sessions</li>
                  <li>• Enable multimedia content</li>
                </ul>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 mt-3 text-white/90">Examples:</h4>
                <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm ml-4">
                  <li>• Language preferences</li>
                  <li>• Font size and accessibility settings</li>
                  <li>• Video player preferences</li>
                  <li>• Chat widget preferences</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">3. Third-Party Cookies</h2>

        <p class="text-white/85 mb-6">
          Some cookies on our website are set by third-party services that appear on our pages. We have no control over these cookies, and they are subject to the respective third party's privacy policy.
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">ZRM CRM</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-3 text-sm">Our CRM and marketing automation platform</p>
            <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm">
              <li>• Form submission tracking</li>
              <li>• Lead capture and management</li>
              <li>• Marketing automation workflows</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="https://zeromotion.marketing/privacy" class="text-primary hover:underline text-sm mt-2 inline-block">View Our Privacy Policy →</a>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Google Services</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-3 text-sm">Analytics, advertising, and performance</p>
            <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm">
              <li>• Website analytics (Google Analytics)</li>
              <li>• Advertising retargeting (Google Ads)</li>
              <li>• Performance monitoring</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-primary hover:underline text-sm mt-2 inline-block">View Privacy Policy →</a>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Facebook</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-3 text-sm">Social media advertising and insights</p>
            <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm">
              <li>• Audience building and targeting</li>
              <li>• Campaign performance measurement</li>
              <li>• Social media integration</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy" class="text-primary hover:underline text-sm mt-2 inline-block">View Privacy Policy →</a>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">LinkedIn</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-3 text-sm">Professional networking and B2B advertising</p>
            <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-1 text-sm">
              <li>• Professional audience targeting</li>
              <li>• Lead generation insights</li>
              <li>• Professional content marketing</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy" class="text-primary hover:underline text-sm mt-2 inline-block">View Privacy Policy →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">4. Managing Your Cookie Preferences</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Cookie Settings Tool</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
              The easiest way to manage your cookie preferences is through our built-in cookie settings tool:
            </p>
            <ol class="text-white/85 space-y-2 ml-4">
              <li>1. Click "Cookie Settings" in the website footer</li>
              <li>2. Review each cookie category and toggle preferences</li>
              <li>3. Save your preferences</li>
              <li>4. Refresh the page to apply changes</li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Browser Settings</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
              You can also control cookies through your browser settings:
            </p>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Chrome</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Settings → Privacy → Cookies</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Firefox</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Preferences → Privacy → Cookies</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Safari</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Preferences → Privacy → Manage Website Data</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 mb-2 text-white/90">Edge</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Settings → Cookies and site permissions</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-yellow-500/10 p-4 rounded-lg">
              <p class="text-white/85 text-sm">
                <strong>Note:</strong> Disabling cookies may affect website functionality. Essential cookies cannot be disabled as they are required for basic site operation.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="h4 mb-4 text-primary">Opt-Out Links</h3>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
              You can opt-out of specific third-party cookies using these direct links:
            </p>
            <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-2">
              <li><a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-primary hover:underline">Google Analytics Opt-out</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://www.facebook.com/ads/preferences" class="text-primary hover:underline">Facebook Advertising Opt-out</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/psettings/advertising" class="text-primary hover:underline">LinkedIn Advertising Opt-out</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" class="text-primary hover:underline">Digital Advertising Alliance Opt-out</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">5. Cookie Retention</h2>

        <div class="card p-6">
          <p class="text-white/85 mb-6">
            Cookies have different lifespans depending on their purpose and type:
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-4 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg">
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 text-primary">Session Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Deleted when you close your browser</p>
              </div>
              <span class="text-white/90 font-semibold">Temporary</span>
            </div>

            <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-4 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg">
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 text-primary">Essential Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Typically 1 year or until consent withdrawn</p>
              </div>
              <span class="text-white/90 font-semibold">1 Year</span>
            </div>

            <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-4 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg">
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 text-primary">Analytics Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Up to 26 months for trend analysis</p>
              </div>
              <span class="text-white/90 font-semibold">26 Months</span>
            </div>

            <div class="flex justify-between items-center p-4 bg-primary/10 rounded-lg">
              <div>
                <h4 class="h5 text-primary">Marketing Cookies</h4>
                <p class="text-white/75 text-sm">Up to 2 years for campaign optimization</p>
              </div>
              <span class="text-white/90 font-semibold">2 Years</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">6. Updates to This Policy</h2>

        <div class="card p-6">
          <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
            We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for other operational, legal, or regulatory reasons.
          </p>

          <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-primary">When We Update:</h3>
          <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-2 mb-4">
            <li>• When we add new cookies or change how existing cookies are used</li>
            <li>• When legal requirements change</li>
            <li>• When we implement new technologies</li>
            <li>• When we modify our privacy practices</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-primary">Notification:</h3>
          <ul class="text-white/85 space-y-2">
            <li>• Updated date at the top of this policy</li>
            <li>• Prominent notice on our website</li>
            <li>• Email notification for significant changes</li>
            <li>• Cookie banner reappearance if needed</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-6 text-primary border-b border-primary/30 pb-2">7. Contact Us</h2>

        <div class="card p-6 bg-primary/10 border-primary/30">
          <p class="text-white/85 mb-4">
            If you have any questions about this Cookie Policy or our use of cookies, please contact us:
          </p>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div>
              <h4 class="h5 mb-3 text-primary">Privacy Team</h4>
              <div class="space-y-2 text-white/85">
                <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:zeromotionmarketing@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">zeromotionmarketing@gmail.com</a></p>
                <p><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+19853032016" class="text-primary hover:underline">(985) 303-2016</a></p>
                <p><strong>Response Time:</strong> Within 5 business days</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h4 class="h5 mb-3 text-primary">Cookie-Specific Support</h4>
              <div class="space-y-2 text-white/85">
                <p><strong>Subject:</strong> "Cookie Policy Inquiry"</p>
                <p><strong>Include:</strong> Browser type and specific concerns</p>
                <p><strong>Technical Support:</strong> Available 9 AM - 5 PM CST</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 p-4 bg-yellow-500/10 border border-yellow-500/30 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-white/85 text-sm">
            <strong>Global Privacy Control:</strong> If you're using a browser with Global Privacy Control (GPC) enabled, we'll automatically respect your privacy preference and limit non-essential cookies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="card p-6 bg-primary/5 border-primary/20">
        <h3 class="h4 mb-3 text-primary">Compliance Standards</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm text-white/75">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-primary/20 rounded-full">GDPR Compliant</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-primary/20 rounded-full">CCPA Compliant</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-primary/20 rounded-full">ePrivacy Directive</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-primary/20 rounded-full">WCAG 2.1 AA Accessible</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-primary/20 rounded-full">Cookie Consent Framework</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
